  "text": "**Solution 2 is wrong.** Its key step fails. For a vector field X = a(w₁₂,w₁₃)∂_{w₁₂} + b∂_{w₁₃}, the commutator [X, e_i] contains the term −e_i(a)∂_{w₁₂}, which is not in D unless e_i(a) = 0. Requiring e₁(a) = e₂(a) = e₃(a) = 0 forces a to be annihilated by all of D. Since D is bracket-generating, such a function is constant. So the proposed infinite family does not preserve D, and the answer ∞ is not supported.\n\n**Solution 3 is unsupported.** It is an explicit recollection-based guess (21, from B₃/P₁,₂), and it does not check any structure of the problem.\n\n**Solution 1 is internally consistent, but I cannot verify its final value.** Its setup checks out:\n- Growth (3,6,8) gives g₋₁ = 3, g₋₂ = 3, g₋₃ = 2.\n- The free level −3 quotient V⊗Λ²V/Λ³V ≅ sl(3) has dimension 8, so g₋₃ = 2 corresponds to a 2-dimensional pencil in sl(3).\n- The grading profile sums correctly: 8 + 7 + (6+3+3+2) = 29.\n\nI cannot run the prolongation computation or check the classification of pencils here, so the value 29 rests on the solution's claims rather than my own verification. Among the three, it is the only one that reasons from the actual structure of the problem, so I take it as the most plausible answer, with low-to-moderate confidence.\n\nCHOICE: 1",
